  "problem": "Let $S$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients and whose degree is greater than or equal to $2.$  Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $f(x)\\in S,$ where $f(x)=2x.$\n\nII. For every $p(x),q(x)\\in S,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)\\in S.$\n\nIII. The set is closed under addition.",
